WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:28.800
Welcome back to Vintage Egyptologist on
YouTube.  We are returning to the Valley

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:36.000
of the Kings to talk about a very
exciting text, the Litany of Re, where we

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.980
will explore some of the fabulous forms
of the sun-god including the great cat

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:51.840
and a jubilating baboon. So the text we
call the Litany of Re, the ancient

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:58.920
Egyptians named the Book of Adoring Re
in the West, is one of the first

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:04.140
attested ancient Egyptian Netherworld
books of the New Kingdom

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:09.000
We call them netherworld books because
we know them primarily from the Valley

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.159
of the Kings, we know them primarily from
the royal tombs of the New Kingdom but

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:20.159
they do appear in temples. There are
examples from the reign of Ramses II in

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:25.439
the temple of Abydos so these might have
been texts that you use in everyday life, at

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:31.290
least by priests, not just in tombs.  A
number of the texts we call the

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.790
Netherworld Books do have passages that
refer to them as having some

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:42.600
applicability for a person on earth and
the Litany of Re itself actually has an

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.990
introductory section that describes how
at least part of it is to be laid out in

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:55.290
registers so the the actual laying out
of these texts probably has a sort of

00:01:55.290 --> 00:02:01.649
ritual function at least in in origin so
people would be drawing these images

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:06.390
from the Litany of Re, writing out the
text and that's part of the ritual,

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.440
this is part of how it all works.
That's probably the case at least for a

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.530
lot of these texts. So we have to
remember for the ancient Egyptians

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:19.319
these are not so much books to be
consulted, to be taken out and checked

00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:26.760
for points of controversy or a point of
religious practice etc but these are

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:34.410
texts the laying out of which and the
reciting of which is part of what we

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:41.220
would call a magical actualization of
the texts. The first examples of the

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:46.610
Litany of Re appear in the tomb of
Thutmose III the and his Vizier Useramun.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:51.150
just to give you a bit of historical
background Thutmose IIIis often

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:56.220
called the Napoleon of ancient Egypt
because he led successful military

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:02.280
campaigns up to the banks of the
Euphrates so in the tomb of Thutmose the

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:08.459
third, the Book of Adoring Re in the
West, the litany of Re, appears elements

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:13.890
of it appear within the decoration of the
tomb, within the chambers of the tomb, but

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:19.519
the text as a whole appears on the
shroud of Thutmose III, a

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:23.640
composition wrapped around the mummy
that would have been endowed by his son

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:30.390
and successor Amenhotep II. After these
double appearances in the tomb of

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.870
Thutmose III and its almost
contemporaneous appearance in the tomb

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:37.890
of his Vizier Useramun we don't
find the Litany of Re in the Valley of

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:44.400
the Kings again until the tomb of the
second ruler of the 19th dynasty the

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:50.549
tomb of Seti the first, probably the the
gem of the Valley of the Kings. He's the

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:55.799
father of Ramses the second (Ramses
the great), one of the most beautifully

00:03:55.799 --> 00:04:03.480
carved structures really in Egypt. The
Litany of Re appears there early in the

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:10.890
19th dynasty and is more or less present
in virtually all of the tombs of the Ramesside

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:16.530
period. In the end it appears as
excerpts in the tombs of Ramses the

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:21.770
ninth and Rameses the tenth so almost at
the very end of the Ramesside period

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:26.470
traditionally it occurs in the first two
descending

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:32.860
passageways of the tomb. We have a plan
of the tomb of Ramses the fourth on a

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:39.630
papyrus that's now in the Turin
Egyptian Museum, and on that papyrus the

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:46.510
entrance corridors of the tomb are
labeled as the pathway of light the way

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:51.670
of Shu,
so the name the area of the tomb in

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:57.820
which the outer daylight might easily
access is the area in which we find

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:04.810
these addresses to the forms of the Sun
god Ra. When you walk into the tomb you

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:10.720
see this to the left and to the right,
often there are scenes sometimes of the

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:17.800
King offering to a god like Ra-horakhty or the four-headed ram that's

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:23.290
definitely the Mendesian Ram form that
appears a little bit later in the later

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:27.790
Ramesside Period.  We'll have to do a an entire episode - he's

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:34.270
exciting: four heads on one
neck, it's great great story and when you

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:41.140
walk in then to the initial sloping
corridor you see what we call the Great

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:48.190
Litany and these are addresses to the
seventy five forms of the Sun God some

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:54.970
of these are male forms like the god Shu
himself or Horus but others are

00:05:54.970 --> 00:06:01.360
goddesses.  So the Sun God can be Tefnut
or Isis or Nephthys and to tackle this

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:07.900
rather complicated text we're going to
start with an address to the great cat

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:14.110
Okay now we're going to look at some of
the 75 addresses - we don't really

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:19.000
have time to look at all of them even in
several episodes so today we're going to

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:25.240
start off with one that Colleen
particularly likes, the 56th address -

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:33.479
it starts off like all with "hekenu en ek Ra" hail to you, Re,

00:06:33.479 --> 00:06:41.440
high and mighty and here it addresses
"miw" and there's a fabulous

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:47.090
determinative of a seated cat so we not
only see the determinative of the cat

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:52.240
here in the hieroglyphic word but we
also see the picture of the cat

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:58.340
illustrating the Great Litany and then
an adjective that follows the word "miw"

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:05.930
for cat is "a-a" that means great.  So you
can see in the first word here "hekenu"

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:14.990
we have the second H, the twisted flax
that seems to be the wick of a candle

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:24.260
the k-basket, the horizontal water sign
for n, then we get the nw-pot and the

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:31.610
quail chick for "w" these are all
phonetic signs, 4 of them are uni

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:37.940
literal signs with one phoneme as a
value the nw-pot is a biliteral with

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:46.000
two phonemes "nw" and following
that group of "hekenu" we get then a

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:53.960
signifier or a determiner as it's called
a determinative and this one is the book

00:07:53.960 --> 00:08:00.500
roll so it is a scroll of papyrus tied
up and that indicates often things that

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:06.620
represent concepts which is interesting
that here praise because it's not the

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:12.230
act of adoration which you normally see
a man with his hands raised in front of

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:17.330
him as they determined him for praise
instead here it's the concept of praise

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.990
probably because they're talking about
the text itself so this is one of the

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:25.250
important features of Egyptian script we
have uniliteral signs that represent one

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:29.990
phoneme, we have biliterals like the nw-pot
here that represent two phonemes

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:36.080
and then we have some triliterals that
represent three phonemes so there's the

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:43.430
scarab beetle for "kheper" There
are a number of forms in the Great

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:50.329
Litany relate to Khepry, there is even Kheprer, he who manifests, and in our

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:54.740
next episode we're going to be talking
about the introductory scene of the

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:58.790
Litany of Re, where within the solar
disk is a ram-headed man and the

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:07.630
scarab beetle as a representation of the
totality of the solar cycle so we get

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:14.360
"Hail to you high and mighty,"
another great determinative here with "qA"

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:24.350
it's a man with his arms raised up so
the motion of raising or exalting so one

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.660
of the things I always point out to
people when they ask why the Egyptians

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:30.620
don't adopt just an alphabetic script.
We will talk about that later,

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:36.200
the alphabetic scripts we know today
develop out of an abgab script so

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:41.480
basically alphabets without the vowels
coming from Egyptian script but the

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:46.880
Egyptians don't adopt that because using
these signifiers, these determinatives

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:54.110
allows them to indicate even aspects of
emotion, concepts behind the word that

00:09:54.110 --> 00:10:00.140
might attach to a specific meaning of a
particular word in a way that an

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:05.570
alphabetic script simply cannot write. So
the Egyptians are able to write on

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:09.380
multiple levels at once - essentially
that's why their script works so

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:13.070
beautifully. So we have the general
introduction "Hail to you, Re, high and

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:20.120
mighty." Then we have a series of epithets
so after the name "miw a-a," the great cat

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:25.760
which is the name of the form of the God
exactly so so the way these litanies are

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:29.959
arranged is we get the introductory
praise then we get essentially an

00:10:29.959 --> 00:10:35.810
address to that specific name form of
the god then what seemed to be a series

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:42.410
of epithets that describe the
significance of that form of Re and

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:49.540
then we get a recapitulation of the form
at the end so the first epithet is "nedj

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:56.830
netcheru," protector of the gods and then
"wedja medu"

00:10:56.830 --> 00:11:02.890
is the term for judge and you might
think: What do cats have to do with

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:08.230
judgment? and we can find the answer
in another text in the Book of the Dead

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:15.160
where we have this fabulous depiction of
the Sun God as a cat slaying the chaos

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:22.690
serpent Apep. This is taking place at
Heliopolis at a place of judgment

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:28.330
and usually the cat is managing to hold
a knife and slice into Apep.  I think

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:33.280
there's a nice depiction of that at
Deir el-Medina and one of the tombs of

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:37.470
the workman there.  We can in fact - it's the
tomb of Sennedjem,

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:43.090
right here it's wonderful how the
Metropolitan Museum put so many of these

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:49.060
images available in the public domain
that is absolutely the way things should

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:53.800
be done and the reason why the cat is
holding a knife is because of that same

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:59.320
principle that John was just describing
with determinatives - it indicates a

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:06.190
signifier that the cat is killing, this
cat is slaying and the determinative to

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:12.970
kill or to slay is a knife so rather
than the cat using his claws to attack Apep,

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:19.690
he's using a knife which is a
hieroglyphic determinative illustrating

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:23.920
perfectly what you were saying about
hieroglyphs being able to be read on

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:28.290
multiple levels.  So this is one thing
always to remember for the Egyptians:

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:34.630
texts will evoke an image or an image
will really contain within it something

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:40.600
that is almost an inscription itself or
maybe a reference to other texts so

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:45.660
rather than showing the cat killing that
you can is holding the knife but a

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:51.790
serpent hieroglyph with a knife stuck in
it can be another way of writing up

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:58.420
because he needs to be magically killed
by the knife so it is on the one hand a

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:02.320
kind of a mythological image of a cat
using a knife to kill a snake but at the

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:06.580
same time it's a marriage of an image of
a cat killing a snake with the

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:12.110
hieroglyphic depiction
of the destroyed chaos serpent.  It's amazing

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:15.470
what they can do,
which is why they never give up

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:23.480
hieroglyphs for an alphabetic system. So
then the great cat is referred to as

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:30.430
"hery wedjat," so chief of the
council in the Council of the gods and

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:37.610
"khenty qereret," foremost of the cavern.
It's specifically the sacred cavern here

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:42.740
the qereret djeseret the secret
cavern which is slightly unusual they

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:47.870
don't normally describe the cavern of
the Netherworld or one of the many

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:53.030
caverns of the Netherworld as being
secret or set aside and the term djeser

00:13:53.030 --> 00:14:00.020
in Egyptian of similar to the Latin
for sacred does mean set apart or

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:05.060
clear it can be even used to clear the
road, the road is sacred, the road is

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:13.190
clear after the great cat is called "foremost" of the sacred cavern, we then get a

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:24.500
recapitulation "tut is miw a-a"
indeed you are the corpse of the sacred cat so

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:31.070
in each of these 75 addresses the Sun
God is both that form, the great cat for

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:39.020
example, but also the corpse of that form
so how this works is essentially the

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:44.270
union of Re and Osiris. This is a
concept we'll come back to over and over

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:47.960
again as we look at the Netherworld Books,  although
it's not something you see a lot in

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:52.730
popular presentations of ancient
Egyptian religion but I think you would

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:59.330
agree it's the central mystery of
ancient. This is the "seshta wer"

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:05.350
the great mystery to which a number of
the Netherworld Books make reference,

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:13.370
essentially the Sun God as he descends
into the Netherworld is described, let's

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:19.480
say in the Book of the Hidden Chamber
that we call him "iwf" flesh

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:24.310
just the corpse as the husk of the Sun must
be rejuvenated

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:31.990
there are encounters between Re and
Osiris in another world and as we know

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:37.120
from The Book of the Dead and from a
text in the tomb of Ramses the Ninth, Re

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:44.709
can be considered tomorrow and Osiris
yesterday together. They're coming

00:15:44.709 --> 00:15:49.060
together, the singularity of the union of
Re and Osiris brings about the new

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:55.269
creation,
so Osiris can personify certain aspects

00:15:55.269 --> 00:16:01.720
of the Netherworld aspects of divinity
by being a corpse the "khat" which is a

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:08.470
feminine word - Osiris can embody other
aspects of a unified deity that can be

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:14.829
seen as feminine, so the "akhet," horizon
can be Osiris so Osiris reclines on the

00:16:14.829 --> 00:16:18.730
horizon as we see at the end of the
twelfth hour of the Book of the Hidden Chamber and

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:25.199
as we see in the enigmatic wall and the
tomb of Ramses the Ninth.  Lots and lots of

00:16:25.199 --> 00:16:31.029
complexity, but once you get some of
these fundamental principles in that

00:16:31.029 --> 00:16:37.120
Egyptian religion at its heart is a
solar religion and the Sun god Re in the

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:42.569
heavens who travels through the
netherworld in the 12 hours of the night

00:16:42.569 --> 00:16:49.269
unifies with his corpse as John
was just discussing unifies with the

00:16:49.269 --> 00:16:55.060
corpse who is Osiris in the afterlife
and these are principles that are so

00:16:55.060 --> 00:17:01.180
rarely explained that once you start
looking out for them if you pick up a

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:05.970
translation of the Pyramid Texts or the
Coffin Texts or the Book the Dead,

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:12.280
especially the Netherworld Books you can
start to see how central this concept is.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:18.939
So even when the Sun God is the great
cat slaying the serpent Apep in the Book

00:17:18.939 --> 00:17:24.880
of the Dead or the great cat who is the
judge or the chief of the council here

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:29.620
in the Litany of Re, you're getting it
something essential about ancient

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.930
Egyptian religion.
So in the netherworld books you'll read

00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:40.060
the "ba demedjy," the unified ba in the
Litany in the addresses to Re you will

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:48.130
find a reference to something called the
"djeba demedj," the unified sarcophagus

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:54.030
form, unified enclosed one - this is one of
those cases where we still don't know

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:58.660
exactly how to translate it and as we
presented on Instagram this week even

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:05.020
just looking at material in books you
can have two images right in front of

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:10.450
each other that you've never seen
juxtaposed and figure out what's going

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:15.790
on so there's so much left to discover
just in books. So let's look at another of

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:19.900
the addresses so we've looked at one
Colleen likes, so let's look at one of which

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:24.970
I'm particularly fond, and that's the
baboon that's the one about the baboons

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:31.870
Now we're going to look at the 69th
address to write so it begins as all the

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:40.180
others "hekenu en ek ra, qa sekhem, "hecka and
that is followed by the word "iany" which

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:47.280
is baboon but the baboon is doing
something particular "hedjen"

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:55.990
jubilating, and this is the idea of
baboons worshiping the Sun God when he

00:18:55.990 --> 00:19:03.760
rises and this relates to one of our
favorite depictions in any Egyptian

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:10.000
temple which is the Solar Chapel of
Medinet Habu.  So in the solar Chapel in

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.020
the right rear of the great mortuary
temple of Ramses the third of Medinet

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:18.100
Habu, if you walk into the temple you go
into the temple proper and go to the

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:21.760
right you'll find the Solar Chapel
you'll actually find a solar chapel

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:25.420
there in most New Kingdom and later
Egyptian temples. This is something we'll

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:29.680
go into when we discuss temple
architecture in Egypt but you'll see

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:35.590
there the souls of the eastern horizon
whom the Egyptians imagined as having

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:40.630
the forms of baboons worshipping the
Rising Sun rearing up and raising their

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:43.040
hands, as
baboons would do as the Sun would come

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:52.490
up and with the baboons is the king
because in the text known as the king as

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:59.330
solar priest this sort of compendium of
syncopated versions of the various sorts

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:03.650
of knowledge that the king is supposed
to possess is the high priest of the Sun

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:09.440
is the chief priest of the solar cult
the king is said to know this language

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:15.740
that the Eastern Souls chatter as they
worship Re so this mysterious language

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:21.080
of the baboons is something that the
Egyptian ruler is supposed to know. Not

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:26.840
only do Egyptian gods have the ability
to assume an animal form but this idea

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:31.640
of animals representing certain concepts
is something we find really with the

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:35.990
dawn of writing in Egypt between about
3500 and 3250

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:40.940
BCE
so it persists in Egyptian religion if

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:45.920
you go all the way back to cat humor in
ancient Egypt if we talk about the baboon

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:52.760
as a form of the god Thoth he is the
monkey who goes into Nubia to bring back

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:59.180
the goddess so when you see a baboon in
an ancient Egyptian scene you don't know

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:03.590
if you're looking at Thoth, if you were
looking at a soul from the eastern

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:10.520
horizon or if you're even looking at a
baboon worshipping Re in the company of

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:15.500
the king which is why it's so important
to be able to read the hieroglyphic text

